#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md:1
#: 2191e3bd122d42c3b657be8c9aec580c
msgid "Network DEA: Coordinating Processes and Assigning Performance Responsibility"
msgstr "网络 DEA：协调组织过程与界定绩效责任"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md:3
#: 313281bd11744874ace95258d1cf280c
msgid ""
"A research institute can be judged as a black box: research staff and "
"budgets enter, while commercial and social results leave. That comparison "
"may answer whether the institute as a whole uses more resources than "
"comparable institutes. It cannot say whether the measured shortfall arises "
"while creating innovations or while turning those innovations into practical"
" outcomes."
msgstr "一家研究机构可以作为黑箱来评价：研究人员和经费投入其中，商业与社会成果从中产出。这种比较或许能够判断该机构整体是否比同类机构耗用更多资源，却无法说明测得的绩效不足发生在创新创造阶段，还是把创新转化为实际成果的阶段。"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md:9
#: 473e9bccf7d94083af009604ab6bdcfa
msgid ""
"Opening the black box changes the question. Patents and prototypes are "
"results of research, but they are also commitments handed to the "
"commercialization process. A credible benchmark must respect both roles at "
"once. It cannot let the research process promise one quantity while the "
"commercialization process plans to receive another incompatible quantity."
msgstr "打开黑箱会改变研究问题。专利和原型是研究过程的成果，也是向商业化过程作出的交付承诺。可信的标杆方案必须同时尊重这两种角色：不能让研究过程承诺一个数量，商业化过程却计划接收另一个不相容的数量。"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md:15
#: 8f717568111240f3a6aca5c810f0bf1c
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Network DEA is the family of models built around this connected "
"organizational question "
"{cite:p}`fare2000network,kao2014,cook2014networkhandbook`. The graph shows "
"how work is organized. The performance measure then reflects whether the "
"study needs only an organization-level score, a relational view of linked "
"process performance, or an additive attribution across processes. Those are "
"different ways to evaluate a connected production system, not "
"interchangeable names for one algorithm."
msgstr ""
"网络数据包络分析（网络 DEA）是一类围绕这种相互联结的组织问题建立的模型 "
"{cite:p}`fare2000network,kao2014,cook2014networkhandbook`。过程图说明工作如何组织，绩效测度则取决于研究需要的是组织层面的单一效率值、相互联结过程绩效的关系型解释，还是跨过程的加性归属。这些是评价一个联结生产系统的不同方式，并非同一算法的不同名称。"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md:23
#: 8cb2c15ec484472481cfabad5ab92050
msgid "What is lost when the organization is treated as one box?"
msgstr "把组织视为一个黑箱会损失什么？"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md:25
#: 3c8ff22b20804e448382e942a0f67ddc
msgid ""
"Suppose organization $j$ uses external resources $x_j$, creates an internal "
"handoff $z_j$, and delivers final outcomes $y_j$:"
msgstr "假设组织 $j$ 使用外部资源 $x_j$，形成内部交付 $z_j$，并提供最终成果 $y_j$："

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md:28
#: 62e29f1fcf9448bf8f27090766090854
msgid ""
"\n"
"x_j \\longrightarrow z_j \\longrightarrow y_j.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"x_j \\longrightarrow z_j \\longrightarrow y_j.\n"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md:32
#: d7a0dd683b7e4d3b89a5b3978dabc67e
msgid "Three studies can be constructed from these quantities."
msgstr "利用这些数量，可以构造三类研究。"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md
#: 45f6978ec492443dac0f08596b85a766
msgid "Study"
msgstr "研究类型"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md
#: 5cab4b4ae1744ead82b7e7f4d41b5b0b
msgid "What is modeled"
msgstr "建模内容"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md
#: 170668ee9f7546629fe2932bf945f30a
msgid "Defensible conclusion"
msgstr "可以成立的结论"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md
#: 3cad3b9f01fa427f998a61f8ef6ecd13
msgid "Black-box DEA"
msgstr "黑箱 DEA"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md
#: da4723f507fc4ff7aa9da59902f39396
msgid "only $x\\rightarrow y$ is retained"
msgstr "仅保留 $x\\rightarrow y$"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md
#: 70c8854f7d5a4c15b941ec3944a41a7d
msgid ""
"performance of the complete organization when internal responsibility is "
"deliberately suppressed"
msgstr "有意忽略内部责任时，完整组织的绩效"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md
#: a5707e3feaf94361b8ad780db2c5402f
msgid "Separate process models"
msgstr "分过程模型"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md
#: e8f1cad8450f46ce8fcf7a2eb116542e
msgid "$x\\rightarrow z$ and $z\\rightarrow y$ are fitted independently"
msgstr "分别拟合 $x\\rightarrow z$ 与 $z\\rightarrow y$"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md
#: 0bb3ce23b0864abaabfb174f01c64689
msgid ""
"how each process compares under its own unconstrained plan; the two plans "
"need not form one feasible organization"
msgstr "各过程在自身不受协调约束的方案下如何比较；两个方案未必能组成一个可行组织"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md
#: cca2be6d64064012b1bfbfa97dff4e1b
msgid "Network DEA"
msgstr "网络 DEA"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md
#: 56ca5337198f48cab97d20addd36d002
msgid "$x\\rightarrow z\\rightarrow y$ is fitted as a connected system"
msgstr "把 $x\\rightarrow z\\rightarrow y$ 拟合为一个联结系统"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md
#: d2c21d1d689b48dbb26d2728b6e6e040
msgid ""
"organization and process evidence under an explicit rule that coordinates "
"the handoff"
msgstr "在明确的内部交付协调规则下，形成组织层面与过程层面的证据"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md:40
#: 932fa5e48e6c47feabfd672032d6ee79
msgid ""
"The network design is warranted only when the internal process boundary is "
"meaningful, the handoff is observed consistently, and the comparison "
"organizations operate sufficiently similar systems. A variable included "
"merely because it is available in a database does not become an intermediate"
" product."
msgstr "只有当内部过程边界具有实际意义、内部交付采用一致口径观察，而且被比较组织运行着足够相似的系统时，网络设计才有必要。一个变量不会仅仅因为数据库中恰好有记录，就自然成为中间产品。"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md:46
#: b7d6c1a7205547778a82288849cfc0d4
msgid ""
"The distinction is also unrelated to the statistical use of the phrase *two-"
"stage analysis*, in which efficiency estimates are later related to "
"environmental variables. That is an inference design, not a two-process "
"production network."
msgstr "这里的区别也与统计分析中所谓的*两阶段分析*无关；后者是在得到效率估计值之后，再考察它们与环境变量的关系。那是一种推断设计，而不是包含两个生产过程的网络。"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md:51
#: b4d85139892e4b1d9110fce0b02e6622
msgid "One quantity, two organizational roles"
msgstr "同一个数量，两种组织角色"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md:53
#: bc470a3c170743b2a5150df7c10d9a9a
msgid ""
"An intermediate is stored once. Its economic role is read from the process "
"graph:"
msgstr "中间产品在数据中只存储一次，其经济角色由过程图决定："

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md:56
#: 7bac8bbfb77c4b328e3a1934f83f3e75
msgid "it is an **outgoing link** for the process that creates it;"
msgstr "对创造它的过程而言，它是**流出联结变量**；"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md:57
#: c1e51cceaaba4d9e95dcac2b1a31ef3d
msgid "it is an **incoming link** for the process that receives it; and"
msgstr "对接收它的过程而言，它是**流入联结变量**；并且"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md:58
#: ab39dff9133343ac9b4579c1798449f8
msgid ""
"it is not counted as an additional final achievement of the organization "
"merely because it appears on both sides of the handoff."
msgstr "不能仅仅因为它出现在内部交付的两侧，就把它额外计为组织的最终成果。"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md:61
#: f06e38568ebd4e32a9aa896f5f4adb88
msgid ""
"This is more than tidy data management. Duplicating an intermediate into two"
" unrelated columns would allow the supplier and recipient to be benchmarked "
"against incompatible quantities. Treating it only as a final output would "
"ignore the downstream commitment. Treating it only as a downstream input "
"would erase the upstream work that created it."
msgstr "这不只是数据整理问题。把同一中间产品复制成两个互不关联的变量，会允许供应过程与接收过程分别针对不相容的数量建立标杆。只把它当作最终产出，会忽略下游承诺；只把它当作下游投入，则会抹去创造它的上游工作。"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md:67
#: 9642914ff46d4f03a057898d6de2f507
msgid ""
"For a general process $k$, four roles are enough to describe the basic "
"network boundary:"
msgstr "对于一般过程 $k$，用四种角色就足以描述基本网络边界："

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md
#: 9f0069db8ec14dfe88478a1a273d8deb
msgid "Role at process $k$"
msgstr "过程 $k$ 中的角色"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md
#: dc787fc3b7db4f29a7de26b5e9cfd715
msgid "Organizational meaning"
msgstr "组织含义"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md
#: 5fa460e3481841d8b869c61353d40106
msgid "external input"
msgstr "外部投入"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md
#: 57e0239aa284421da68b927ced6187fb
msgid "a resource enters the organization at this process"
msgstr "资源在该过程进入组织"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md
#: 774875aace7c4ae5be0a2e41ef80fc3c
msgid "incoming link"
msgstr "流入联结变量"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md
#: ea98d2317d114e2cbb1aba314758932e
msgid "work created by another process is received here"
msgstr "由另一过程创造的工作成果在此被接收"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md
#: 886d64fae2b54fc2aef0885a3a880a34
msgid "external output"
msgstr "外部产出"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md
#: 8c8cdeb04dd340179d5510deab7bf05b
msgid "a result leaves the organization here"
msgstr "成果在该过程离开组织"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md
#: c6c4d4aa5b184a719a5637977805ed40
msgid "outgoing link"
msgstr "流出联结变量"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md
#: dd3ed8078aa04eb7a8d3099da6efb2e4
msgid "work remains inside the organization and is handed onward"
msgstr "工作成果仍留在组织内部，并继续交付给下一过程"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md:77
#: e06b7a414f344f8fbb1154db80748a53
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"A closed two-stage chain places every external resource before the first "
"process and every final result after the second. Many organizations are "
"open: a later process receives new staff, an early process releases a final "
"service, or different internal streams branch and rejoin. The location of "
"those boundary crossings assigns resources and results to the managers and "
"processes that actually use or create them {cite:p}`cook2010additive`."
msgstr ""
"封闭的两阶段链把所有外部资源置于第一过程之前，把所有最终成果置于第二过程之后。许多组织则是开放的：后续过程可能获得新增人员，前序过程可能直接提供最终服务，不同内部流也可能分支后再汇合。边界穿越发生在哪里，就把资源和成果归入实际使用或创造它们的管理者与过程"
" {cite:p}`cook2010additive`。"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md:84
#: 835d945009694da4908e21aabd961fb7
msgid ""
"A closed two-process chain is contrasted with an open network in which "
"resources enter and outcomes leave at several processes while internal links"
" branch, rejoin, or skip a process"
msgstr "封闭的两过程链与开放网络的对比：在开放网络中，资源可以从多个过程进入，成果也可以从多个过程离开，内部联结则可以分支、汇合或跨越某一过程"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md:89
#: b4f3aef9d56842e7a95cfa622f222aab
msgid ""
"A process graph defines the organizational boundary before performance is "
"calculated; it is not decoration added after the scores are known."
msgstr "过程图在计算绩效之前界定组织边界，而不是在效率值已知后添加的装饰。"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md:93
#: f545d3cc18c04c4fa75ba39ea2d4fac1
msgid ""
"A connection in the graph records an organizational dependence: one process "
"must deliver something that another process needs in order to operate. If "
"research supplies a patent to commercialization, the model requires their "
"benchmark plans to agree on that handoff. It does not establish how long "
"commercialization takes or that the research manager caused a later sale. "
"The managerial content lies in coordinating the shared commitment, not in "
"the direction of an arrow on the page."
msgstr "图中的一条连接记录了一项组织依赖：一个过程必须交付另一过程开展工作所需要的内容。如果研究过程向商业化过程提供专利，模型就要求二者的标杆方案对这一交付量保持一致。它既不能说明商业化需要多长时间，也不能证明研究管理者造成了后续销售。其管理含义来自对共享承诺的协调，而不是纸面上箭头的方向。"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md:100
#: 4b900594e4ae46bf89e1a14bf6b31efd
msgid "Different processes may learn from different peers"
msgstr "不同过程可以向不同参照单元学习"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md:102
#: 238254094d5a4452ad93f352a388188b
msgid ""
"Opening the organization does not require every process to imitate the same "
"reference organization. Let $\\lambda$ describe the peer plan for research "
"and $\\mu$ the peer plan for commercialization. When management protects the"
" final service commitment and asks how much external resource can be "
"released, the coordinated system model is"
msgstr ""
"打开组织黑箱，并不要求每个过程都模仿同一个参照组织。令 $\\lambda$ 表示研究过程的参照方案，$\\mu$ "
"表示商业化过程的参照方案。当管理层要保护最终服务承诺，并考察能够释放多少外部资源时，协调后的系统模型为"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md:108
#: c81f2acfe991478498b61e540da81659
msgid ""
"\n"
"X\\lambda\\leq \\theta_o x_o,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"Z\\lambda\\geq Z\\mu,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"Y\\mu\\geq y_o.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"X\\lambda\\leq \\theta_o x_o,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"Z\\lambda\\geq Z\\mu,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"Y\\mu\\geq y_o.\n"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md:116
#: 6cfb1639975d428380244be0ef66d44d
msgid ""
"Here $\\theta_o$ is the proportion of the focal organization's external-"
"resource commitment required by the coordinated benchmark. The upstream plan"
" may learn from one set of organizations and the downstream plan from "
"another. What makes the result one organizational plan is the link "
"condition: research can supply at least what commercialization requires."
msgstr ""
"这里，$\\theta_o$ "
"表示协调标杆为完成任务所需保留的焦点组织外部资源承诺比例。上游方案可以向一组组织学习，下游方案可以向另一组组织学习。使结果成为同一个组织方案的是联结条件：研究过程能够提供至少满足商业化过程所需的数量。"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md:122
#: d6f6b48ac06c450892520ae9dd25b8d4
msgid ""
"If the current resource commitment is the binding management constraint, the"
" same system can instead ask how far final services could expand:"
msgstr "如果当前资源承诺是管理上不可突破的约束，同一系统也可以转而考察最终服务能够扩张到何种程度："

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md:125
#: 3eb510432cbd44ec8dd6e39f3abe8d95
msgid ""
"\n"
"X\\lambda\\leq x_o,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"Z\\lambda\\geq Z\\mu,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"Y\\mu\\geq \\phi_o y_o.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"X\\lambda\\leq x_o,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"Z\\lambda\\geq Z\\mu,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"Y\\mu\\geq \\phi_o y_o.\n"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md:133
#: b6115fdb08954500ac6714d47d1c2242
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The largest feasible $\\phi_o$ is the service-expansion factor, and the "
"higher-is-better output efficiency is $1/\\phi_o$. This output-distance "
"formulation comes from the same intermediate-products network lineage "
"{cite:p}`fare1996intermediate`; it is an orientation of the same core "
"family, not another model. Choosing between $\\theta_o$ and $\\phi_o$ "
"records what management promises to hold fixed: final services in the first "
"case, or the external resource commitment in the second."
msgstr ""
"最大可行的 $\\phi_o$ 是服务扩张因子，数值越高越好的产出效率为 $1/\\phi_o$。这一产出距离表述源于同一中间产品网络研究脉络 "
"{cite:p}`fare1996intermediate`；它只是同一核心模型族的另一种导向，而不是另一种模型。在 $\\theta_o$ 与 "
"$\\phi_o$ 之间作出选择，记录了管理层承诺保持不变的对象：前者固定最终服务，后者固定外部资源承诺。"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md:141
#: 7eb7ac0ceeb44a098fa1ad54f84a53bb
msgid ""
"The difference $Z\\lambda-Z\\mu$ is a disposable internal surplus under this"
" particular system technology. It is not automatically waste attributable to"
" the supplying process. It may reflect timing, quality, risk buffers, "
"indivisibilities, omitted constraints, or an alternative optimum. Other "
"network models impose equality or attach a scored responsibility to a link; "
"the appropriate condition belongs to the technology assumptions and "
"performance question."
msgstr ""
"在这一特定系统技术下，差额 $Z\\lambda-Z\\mu$ "
"是可自由处置的内部盈余，不能自动解释为应归责于供应过程的浪费。它可能反映时点差异、质量差异、风险缓冲、不可分性、遗漏约束或多重最优解。其他网络模型可能要求严格相等，或把联结偏差计入某个责任账户；应采用何种条件，取决于生产技术假设和绩效问题。"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md:149
#: d704d8d6c12d40f681c27355c0739eb0
msgid "Two principles carry across the family:"
msgstr "整个模型族都应遵守两项原则："

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md:151
#: fd3cfbb825954f75bdbc36e389fa449a
msgid "process-specific peers must coexist in one feasible organization; and"
msgstr "各过程特有的参照方案必须能够在同一个可行组织中共存；以及"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md:152
#: d113f6b664c6483abba3392352c0d001
msgid "common link accounting does not imply common peer coefficients."
msgstr "共同的联结核算并不意味着各过程必须使用相同的参照强度变量。"

#: ../../chapters/05-network/network-dea-organizations-links-responsibility.md:154
#: 4038c9a66bf94d9ab2ef99b567508b83
